**continue Statement:**

**Purpose:** **Skips** the rest of the current iteration and moves to the **next** iteration.

**continue vs break:**

```java
// break: exits loop completely
for (int i = 1; i <= 5; i++) {
    if (i == 3) break;
    System.out.print(i + " ");
}
// Output: 1 2

// continue: skips to next iteration
for (int i = 1; i <= 5; i++) {
    if (i == 3) continue;
    System.out.print(i + " ");
}
// Output: 1 2 4 5 (skips 3)
```

**Common Use Cases:**

1. **Skip Specific Values:**
```java
// Print odd numbers only
for (int i = 1; i <= 10; i++) {
    if (i % 2 == 0) {
        continue;  // Skip even numbers
    }
    System.out.print(i + " ");  // 1 3 5 7 9
}
```

2. **Skip Invalid Data:**
```java
int[] numbers = {5, -2, 10, -7, 15, -3, 20};
int sum = 0;

for (int num : numbers) {
    if (num < 0) {
        continue;  // Skip negative numbers
    }
    sum += num;  // Only add positive numbers
}
// sum = 50 (5 + 10 + 15 + 20)
```

3. **Skip Empty/Null:**
```java
String[] names = {"Alice", "", "Bob", null, "Charlie"};

for (String name : names) {
    if (name == null || name.isEmpty()) {
        continue;  // Skip invalid names
    }
    System.out.println(name);
}
// Prints: Alice, Bob, Charlie
```

**How It Works:**
