**Top Loop Mistakes:**

**1. Infinite Loop - Forgot to Update Counter:**
```java
// ❌ WRONG
int i = 1;
while (i <= 10) {
    System.out.println(i);
    // Forgot i++!
}

// ✅ CORRECT
int i = 1;
while (i <= 10) {
    System.out.println(i);
    i++;  // Must update
}
```

**2. Off-by-One Error:**
```java
// ❌ WRONG - 11 iterations
for (int i = 0; i <= 10; i++) { }

// ✅ CORRECT - 10 iterations
for (int i = 0; i < 10; i++) { }

// ❌ WRONG - Missing last element
for (int i = 0; i < arr.length - 1; i++) { }

// ✅ CORRECT
for (int i = 0; i < arr.length; i++) { }
```

**3. Accidental Semicolon:**
```java
// ❌ WRONG - Empty loop body
for (int i = 0; i < 10; i++);  // Semicolon!
{
    System.out.println(i);  // Error: i not in scope
}

// ✅ CORRECT
for (int i = 0; i < 10; i++) {
    System.out.println(i);
}
```

**4. Modifying Array in for-each:**
```java
// ❌ WRONG - Doesn't modify array
for (int num : arr) {
    num = num * 2;  // Only modifies copy!
}

// ✅ CORRECT - Use indexed loop
for (int i = 0; i < arr.length; i++) {
    arr[i] = arr[i] * 2;
}
```

**5. Wrong Update Direction:**
```java
// ❌ WRONG - Infinite loop
for (int i = 10; i > 0; i++) {  // Incrementing!
    System.out.println(i);
}

// ✅ CORRECT
for (int i = 10; i > 0; i--) {  // Decrementing
    System.out.println(i);
}
```

**6. Using length() Instead of length:**
```java
// ❌ WRONG
for (int i = 0; i < arr.length(); i++) { }  // Error!

// ✅ CORRECT
for (int i = 0; i < arr.length; i++) { }  // No ()
```

